    "body": "This is also noted in https://github.com/whatwg/compression/issues/39#issuecomment-3193971195.\n\nGecko [bails out without enqueuing when the stream end is met](https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/30ea9a2fd7271e9c731df414bd80e46edc3190eb/dom/base/DecompressionStream.cpp#195-207), and [same for WebKit](https://searchfox.org/wubkat/rev/45ea2913aecbb396d34759db76ce6a8d9045bf31/Source/WebCore/Modules/compression/DecompressionStreamDecoder.cpp#155-156). But [Blink still enqueues](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/modules/compression/inflate_transformer.cc;l=147-160;drc=31007e87feb834e9b5dc3047cb03055949a7a198).\n\nMozilla is open to change the implementation (seems more useful to me too), but the spec change/clarification and WPT coverage should be made.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
