    "created_at": "2025-09-25T22:39:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-25T22:39:58Z",
    "body": "> Let buffer be the result of decompressing chunk with ds’s [format](https://compression.spec.whatwg.org/#decompressionstream-format) and [context](https://compression.spec.whatwg.org/#decompressionstream-context). If this results in an error, then throw a [TypeError](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#exceptiondef-typeerror).\n\nI think both Gecko and WebKit probably are treating \"Z_STREAM_END with any remaining data\" as an error condition. But Z_STREAM_END itself is not an error. Perhaps the spec is fine as-is but we just need WPT coverage?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
